Changelog: 16-10-2026 11:35:40

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 16-10-2026 11:20:26

Added. New app vita3k-manager (Vita3K Manager): PS Vita games on the BC-250 with the Vita3K emulator, built as the
RPCS3 Manager is (owner, 16-10-2026). Install downloads Vita3K build 4186 (0.2.1, commit f0273e4c), the build the app
pins: Vita3K-x86_64.AppImage from that build's release in Vita3K/Vita3K-builds, checked against its SHA-256 (the
digest GitHub publishes for it) and installed in ~/.local/share/bc250-vita3k-manager/emulator as vita3k.AppImage,
with "current" pointing to it; Remove takes it out, Vita3K's own folders (~/.config/Vita3K, and the storage in
~/.local/share/Vita3K/Vita3K or where config.yml's pref-path puts it) stay. When the window opens, the app asks
GitHub for Vita3K's newest build (Vita3K-builds' latest release, tagged with its number) and says when it is newer,
with a link; it installs only the build it was tried with. The firmware step shows the three parts of the PS Vita's
firmware as Vita3K counts them (the system software in vs0, the font package in sa0, the optional preinstalled apps
in pd0), with links to the official firmware page and Sony's two other files, and Install firmware… has Vita3K
install the user's own PSP2UPDAT.PUP without a window (--firmware), then says which part it filled; the app never
downloads the firmware. Install game… (owner, 16-10-2026: in the app) installs the user's own dumps: a .pkg with its
zRIF licence key through Vita3K without a window (--pkg, --zrif), a .vpk, .zip or dumped folder handed to Vita3K,
which installs it and starts it in its own window, the list following once the game is in ux0/app. The games are
those in the storage's ux0/app with eboot.bin and sce_sys/param.sfo (title, ID and version as Vita3K shows them).
Play starts a game alone (--frontend sdl -r <ID>), Vita3K settings opens Vita3K's own window. Update Game Mode adds
the ticked games to Steam as non-Steam games and takes out the others and games no longer installed, with Steam
closed for it and started again (core's bc250_core.steam), named "[PS Vita] Title"; the artwork is drawn from the
game's icon0.png and pic0.png, with icon0.png as the logo. The shortcuts run bc250-vita3k-run --frontend sdl -r
<ID>: Vita3K's plain SDL window, which quits with the game, without --fullscreen (Vita3K would write it into its
config.yml for its own window too). The run wrapper starts the installed Vita3K, turns off the AppImage's own
self-updater (DISABLE_AUTO_UPDATES=1: it would write the newest continuous build over itself), lets the AppImage
unpack itself when there is no fusermount, and, as the RPCS3 Manager's, has Vita3K read a real controller instead of
Steam's virtual one when Steam starts it, and open its windows through XWayland (SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER=x11,
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb) when Steam starts it on a Wayland desktop. Should the AppImage have been replaced all the same,
the app sees it by the file's size and Install puts the pinned build back. The window has its own look in Vita3K's
crimson #BD1550 (style.py). The installer uses the suite's shared venv and installs the wrapper in ~/.local/bin. The
icon is a placeholder until the owner's images are ready. Tests: the config.yml build 4186 writes is a fixture.
